y pay you  to do social impact work over the summer  i was fortunate to receive the social  change leadership award which about  12 to 15 people get when they're  graduating for work on campus related to  social entrepreneurship and there's also  full-time fellowship opportunities  post-graduation  and so a couple of my friends have  received those fellowships that  pay them true full-time you know  post-business school salaries  to run their own um socially impactful  businesses post-grad  and so a plethora of opportunities for  sure  great khalil thank you for sharing that  and actually you brought up a really  important  point which also i saw surface in the  questions  especially considering some folks are  going to be coming from education  non-profit thinking about business  school and knowing that you may be  returning to a non-profit space and you  may not be joining  jp morgan right after graduation uh  certainly financing the nba  is on a lot of people's minds and i  think you mentioned that through the the  social innovation  uh center there are actually  opportunities for  for funding and support both at the  internship level  uh and uh post grad you know as  uh as an alum uh one thing i just want  to mention to the group  um because i know not everyone is is  going into non-profit here on this panel  but we also have a very generous loan  forgiveness program  so i certainly encourage you to check  out our website to learn more there so  if you are planning to go back into the  nonprofit space  there is a loan forgiveness program  through stanford because we really do  believe that we want people to pursue  their passions and pursue the careers  that they want  not just the ones they think they have  to take we don't want anyone to make any  compromises or sacrifices there so just  wanted to  add that point khalil thank you all  right question from  sri here how accessible or approachable  are professors and what is the class  dynamic like is it more col